// GDTF battle keybind table — the FIRST keybind file in the repo (GTW-48 S8 /
// GTW-225). Maps each bound battle ACT to a named key (a `BoundKey` variant that
// resolves to a Bevy KeyCode). Edit freely — every binding is data, hot-swappable
// through the same RonAsset<T> loader the theme / tiles / tuning use; nothing about
// the key choices is hardcoded in Rust. The keyboard systems read the resolved
// KeyCode off the loaded Keybinds resource, never a literal.
//
// `select_clear` / `level_up` / `level_down` are consumed THIS slice (GTW-225);
// `stance_cycle` / `aim_toggle` / `facing_cycle` / `fire_mode_cycle` are declared
// here and consumed by the keyboard act surface (GTW-222b) over the shared intent
// seam — so the act keys live in ONE authoritative table from the start.
(
    select_clear:    KeyEscape,    // clear the current ganger selection
    level_up:        KeyPageUp,    // raise the active storey by one level (clamped to the top)
    level_down:      KeyPageDown,  // lower the active storey by one level (floored at 0)
    stance_cycle:    KeyC,         // step the selected ganger's stance (Standing->Crouching->Prone->wrap) [222b]
    aim_toggle:      KeyF,         // toggle the selected ganger's aim mode [222b]
    facing_cycle:    KeyR,         // step the selected ganger's facing (N->NE->...->NW->wrap) [222b]
    fire_mode_cycle: KeyQ,         // step the selected ganger's fire mode [222b]
)
